  "note": "Arabic ḍ in the rib word and ẓ in the limping verb point to two older roots. The shared spelling of Zelah does not establish the town name’s meaning. The personal names Zelophehad, Zalaph and Zelek and the place name Zelzah are grouped nearby in the catalogue, but the passages give no derivation from either word."
